From 826035f8fd1aae3a1121ab29343ff7bfc697b365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matteo Geromin <geromin.matteo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:04:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] Add video drivers for BeagleBone

Enable DM video support with the AM335x LCD controller (tilcdc) driver
in am335x_evm_defconfig, together with the TI clock drivers (and
regmap) needed by tilcdc to program the LCD pixel clock.

Enabling AM335X_LCD made the EVM LCD pinmux table part of SPL, which
then overflowed SRAM. The LCD is only used by U-Boot proper, so move
the LCD pinmux into mux_lcd.c (built for U-Boot proper only) and
apply it from board_init().

Ported from the 2015 patch, which added the da8xx-fb / cfb_console
Kconfig symbols that no longer exist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
